  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which one of the following graphs is not correct for ideal gas?</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Density,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Pressure,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo></math>Temperature</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0035_8f44b66a4729.png\" style=\"width: 263px; height: 272px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "I&nbsp;&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "II&nbsp;&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "IV&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "III&nbsp;",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For ideal gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>PM</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Graph between density versus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;should be straight line.</p><p>Graph between density versus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math>&nbsp;should be straight line.</p><p>So graph between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi></math> is not straight line.</p><p>Hence option II is wrong.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0035_09413328bdbc.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 127px;\" /></p>"
  }
